ng\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nModel name (e.g., Sonnet 4, Tab…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nRequest ID: f9a7046a-279b-47e5-ab48-6e8dc12daba1\u003cbr\u003e\nFor Background Agent issues, also post the ID: bc-…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"92:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"93:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"94:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe more details you provide, the easier it is for us to reproduce and fix the issue. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere does the bug appear?\u003cbr\u003e\nSomething else: Grok Bot desktop app (Cursor’s assistant app), agent computer / box desktop\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003cbr\u003e\nMy Grok Bot assistant “ToddBot” has lost desktop/browser control. It can still take read-only screenshots of its own box desktop and run shell commands, but the tool that lets it click, type, and scroll in its browser is no longer available in its session. Browser logins on the box are intact; the agent just cannot operate the browser. My other daily workflows (DAT, SONAR, Aljex, Outlook pulls) depend on this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the ToddBot chat in Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAsk it to open a site in its browser and click something.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIt reports it has no desktop-control tool; only screenshot works.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlready tried\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings \u0026gt; Update Grok Bot’s Computer (completed 9/29/2026 ~8:25 AM ET). Files and logins survived; still no browser control.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit and reopened the Grok Bot app (9/29/2026 ~8:30 AM ET). Still missing.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected Behavior\u003cbr\u003e\nThe agent can drive its box desktop/browser (click, type, scroll) as it could before about 9/22/2026.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScreenshots\u003cbr\u003e\n(none; the issue is a missing capability, not a visual error)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOperating System\u003cbr\u003e\n[your OS]; agent box is Linux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion Information\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot app version: 0.61.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eModel\u003cbr\u003e\nNot model-specific\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional Information\u003cbr\u003e\nStarted around 9/22/2026. Affects one agent (ToddBot); not yet confirmed whether other agents on the same account are affected.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003cbr\u003e\nSometimes - core browser workflows are blocked, everything else works\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:35:59.461Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":173319,"topic_slug":"loss-of-browser-control","display_username":"Todd Cunningham","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":140254,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/loss-of-browser-control/173319/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":503501,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:22:37.257Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/todd_cunningham\"\u003e@Todd_Cunningham\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report and for already trying the update and restart.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA bit of background on how this works: Grok Bot’s own screenshot tool is view-only on purpose. When it needs to click, type or browse, it hands that step to a background computer-use helper that drives its desktop. That helper is still available to ToddBot (it’s working normally on your account), but ToddBot has stopped using it and is telling you the tool is gone. That’s also why updating the computer and restarting the app didn’t change anything.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you try this and tell me what happens?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the ToddBot chat in Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend exactly: “Launch a computer-use helper (Task tool, computerUse) to open \u003ca href=\"https://www.google.com\"\u003ehttps://www.google.com\u003c/a\u003e in your browser and click the search box. Don’t reply until it finishes.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait for it to finish without sending another message.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf it works, you can ask ToddBot to always hand browser work to its computer-use helper. If it has saved a note or instruction saying it has no browser control, ask it to remove that note.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf it still says it can’t, please reply with the time you tried (with your time zone) and ToddBot’s exact reply, and I’ll dig in from there.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:22:37.257Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173319,"topic_slug":"loss-of-browser-control","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.google.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Google","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/loss-of-browser-control/173319/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[503396,503397,503401,503501]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":373,"name":"computer-use","slug":"computer-use"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Loss of Browser control","id":173319,"tit